 location="Paravertebral gutter on each side from C1 to the coccyx: cervical ganglia in front of the transverse processes behind the carotid sheath, thoracic ganglia on the heads of the ribs, lumbar ganglia on the vertebral bodies, sacral ganglia medial to the anterior sacral foramina, joining at the ganglion impar.",
 subdivisions=[("Superior cervical ganglion", "C1–C4 level; postganglionic fibers to the head (pupil, lid, face sweating) via the internal carotid plexus"), ("Middle cervical and stellate (cervicothoracic) ganglia", "C6–T1; upper limb, heart"), ("Thoracic ganglia", "cardiac and pulmonary nerves; greater, lesser and least splanchnic nerves to the abdomen"), ("Lumbar and sacral ganglia", "lower limb and pelvic viscera")],
